Title: "`mlg search`"
Id: "3df793a1-1209-4821-b384-cb919241b890"

Text: "`mlg search` searches items and definitions across the current collection.

```text
mlg search [--json] <QUERY>
```

The command scans all `.mlg` files in the collection for matches to the specified query string across item headings, titles, descriptions, and defined command signatures.

In default human-readable mode, `mlg search` prints matching files, items, match reasons, and context snippets.

With `--json`, it outputs a machine-readable JSON object with the following structure:

```text
{
  \"query\": \"search query\",
  \"totalMatches\": 1,
  \"matches\": [
    {
      \"filePath\": \"content/path/to/file.mlg\",
      \"id\": \"uuid-here\",
      \"kind\": \"Defines\",
      \"heading\": \"\\command.name\",
      \"definitionKeys\": [\"\\command.name\"],
      \"matchReasons\": [\"Matched command: \\command.name\"],
      \"snippet\": \"Defines: ...\"
    }
  ]
}
```

The command accepts the global event filters: `--event-audience` (or `--event-scope`), `--event-level`, and `--event-markers`."
Id: "e72e1765-b1a9-4674-8b17-f58c4ca14668"
